/*!
\page page_stEmcRawData StEmcRawData

\brief Raw DAQ data banks for the STAR Electromagnetic Calorimeter (BEMC or EEMC).

\section emcrawdata_overview Overview

StEmcRawData stores the unprocessed DAQ output from the EMC readout
electronics as an array of up to 60 bank objects (one per DAQ crate).  Each
bank consists of a header array (crate/trigger metadata) and a data array
(raw ADC payload words).  The class is the input to the EMC unpacker chain;
most physics analyses use the decoded StEmcRawHit objects instead.

\section emcrawdata_hierarchy Class Hierarchy

\code
TObject → StObject → StEmcRawData
\endcode

Held by \ref page_stEmcCollection "StEmcCollection" (for BEMC and/or EEMC).

\section emcrawdata_members Data Members

| Type | Name | Description |
|---|---|---|
| TArrayS[60] | mHeader | Header word arrays, one per DAQ crate bank (index 0–59). |
| TArrayS[60] | mData | Raw ADC payload arrays, one per DAQ crate bank. |

\c MAXEMCDATABANK = 60 is the maximum number of bank slots.

\section emcrawdata_methods Key Methods

- \c getNBlocks() — total number of bank slots (60).
- \c header(bank) / \c data(bank) — pointer to array for a bank.
- \c header(bank,pos) / \c data(bank,pos) — individual words.
- \c sizeHeader(bank) / \c sizeData(bank) — array sizes.
- \c createBank(bank,nH,nD) — allocate bank arrays.
- \c deleteBank(bank) — release bank arrays.
- \c setHeader() / \c setData() — populate from external buffers.

\section emcrawdata_seealso See Also

\ref page_stEmcRawHit "StEmcRawHit",
\ref page_stEmcDetector "StEmcDetector"
*/
